{"t":1787899611011,"event":{"type":"agent:critique","iteration":1,"defects":["Text critic (severity=medium): I'll review this Account Settings panel design critically, examining all dimensions against the fidelity bar and design standards.\n\n---\n\n## Analysis\n\n**Fidelity (gate)**: This is high-fidelity — has a dark color palette, 4 shapes with shadows, 1 gradient on the Save button, and real domain content (\"Alexandra Chen\", \"alexandra.chen@example.com\"). Not a wireframe.\n\n**Visual hierarchy**: The panel title (20px, #e2e8f0) is appropriately largest. Labels are smallest (12px, muted). However, the Save button uses #6366f1 (indigo) which doesn't appear in the design tokens — this creates a color system inconsistency. The gradient on the button is a nice touch but the color is off-palette.\n\n**Alignment & spacing**: \n- Field containers (\"DisplayNameField\", \"EmailField\") are 336×72 but their child inp","VLM critic (score=4/10, severity=medium):","  - [high] Implement systematic spacing with 8px grid: card padding 32px, label-input gap 8px, field-to-field 24px, button margin-top 32px","  - [high] Add focus, hover, active, and disabled states to all interactive elements with transition-all duration-200","  - [high] Establish color system: derive button from card using indigo family, add semantic colors, fix label contrast to WCAG AA","  - [med] Unify border-radius system (card 16px, inputs/button 8px) and replace heavy shadow with modern subtle shadow","  - [med] Add responsive container (max-w-md, centered) and realistic content expansion (avatar upload, password field, or helper text)"],"validation":{"totalShapes":12,"textShapes":6,"cardShapes":0,"textShapesWithWeight":4,"cardShapesWithShadow":0,"autoLayoutContainers":6},"textSeverity":"medium","vlmSeverity":"medium","vlmScore":4}}
